  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1218 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nMonday Night through Saturday:\n\nThe mid level shortwave trough will begin to deepen as it gets\nover the lower Great Lakes late Monday night. This will usher a\nperiod of gusty northerly winds down Lake Michigan, that will\narrive and push inland from Sheboygan beginning around midnight. \nCooler and drier air will arrive in the wake of this cold front. \nHighs Tuesday will be in the upper 70s near Lake Michigan to the\nlower 80s inland. Dewpoints will drop into the upper 50s to \naround 60 by late afternoon. Lows Tuesday night will be in the\nupper 50s to lower 60s, and patchy fog looks possible.\n\nWith persistent north-northeast winds along the lakeshore, a high\nswim risk will develop for all of the lakeshore counties from\nSheboygan to Kenosha due to waves of 4 to 6 feet. A Beach Hazards\nStatement was issued. This runs for a long time, from late Monday\nnight through late Wednesday morning. High pressure will take hold\nand help winds and waves diminish Wednesday, and the headline may\nbe able to be canceled a little early. \n\nHighs Wednesday will be around 80 near the lakeshore and mid 80s\ninland. Areas toward central WI could see upper 80s once again as\nthe warm and moist ridge starts to push back into the region. By\nWednesday evening, we will be back in an unsettled weather\npattern. A shortwave rounding the ridge over MN and northern WI\nWed nt could generate upstream storms, but the chance of it\npushing all the way into southern WI is low due to the surface\nridge directly overhead. The upper ridge will push into southern \nWI on Thursday, giving us highs in the upper 80s and heat indices \nin the lower 90s. \n\nAnother shortwave will ride over the ridge in the Northern Plains,\nbut amplify as it crosses the Upper Great Lakes on Friday. There\nis fair consensus between the GFS and ECMWF with this feature.\nThis will bring us a chance for showers and a few storms, but \nthere is a lower probability for severe. The trough will slowly \nexit Wisconsin Saturday, with shower chances lingering until then.\nHigh temperatures Friday through the weekend should be in the\nlower 80s. \n\nCronce",
